# Grub, Notorious Auntie (CR 701.68a, 707.2, 707.8a, 508.4, 704.5j): transformed on turn 3, Grub attacks and its controller blights Grub
# itself - a -1/-1 counter on a 2/1. The token is a copy of Grub as it is now, without the counter (CR 707.2), created tapped and
# attacking Bot2 but never declared as an attacker (CR 508.4), so its own "whenever Grub attacks" does not trigger: nothing is on the
# stack and no second blight is offered (! Bot1.Accept). The two Grubs are legendary, so the legend rule has Bot1 keep one (the token);
# the counter-bearing original dies of its toughness 0 either way. The token deals 2 to Bot2 and is sacrificed at the end step.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Grub, Storied Matriarch
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

